#: ../developer/batches.md:1
msgid "Batch Inference"
msgstr "批量推理"

#: ../developer/batches.md:3
msgid ""
"`/v1/batches` takes many chat-completion requests in one call and answers"
" them later. You submit the whole job, poll it, then page through the "
"results. The gateway runs the requests in the background, a few at a time"
" per model, beside its interactive traffic."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:8
msgid ""
"The shapes follow OpenAI's Batch API: batch objects, their statuses and "
"the result lines are the same. Two things differ. The requests travel "
"inline in the create call, because the gateway has no Files API, and the "
"results are read a page at a time rather than downloaded as a file."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:14
msgid ""
"Only **internal** users and administrators can create batches unless the "
"operator opens them to other roles. A gateway with batch inference turned"
" off, or without a database, answers every `/v1/batches` route with "
"`404`."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:19
msgid "How it works"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid ""
"Creating a batch validates every request in it and stores them. Nothing "
"runs during that call: the batch starts as `validating`, and the "
"gateway's worker starts its requests as soon as their models have room."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:25
msgid ""
"Each request then runs exactly as if you had sent it to "
"`/v1/chat/completions` yourself: the same models, routing and fallback, "
"the same price, logged under your account. It counts toward your daily "
"cost quota and takes one of your concurrent-request slots while it runs, "
"so a batch never gets more than your own traffic could. Requests run in "
"no particular order, and a request that fails for a reason that may pass "
"— a timeout, a `429`, a `5xx` — is retried with backoff, up to eight "
"attempts in all. A request the model rejects (any other `4xx`) fails at "
"once."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:34
msgid ""
"Before each request runs, the gateway checks the API key that created the"
" batch again:"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:37
msgid ""
"if the key was revoked or has expired, or the account was suspended or "
"deleted, the batch fails;"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:39
msgid ""
"if your daily quota is used up, your batches pause until it renews at "
"midnight UTC;"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:41
msgid "if your role no longer allows batches, they pause until it does."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:43
msgid "So keep the key you created a batch with until the batch finishes."
msgstr ""

