#: ../developer/batches.md:277
msgid "Cancel or delete a batch"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:279
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`POST /v1/batches/{id}/cancel` stops a batch. Requests that have not "
"started are cancelled; running ones finish and keep their results. The "
"batch is `cancelling` until they do, then `cancelled`. Cancelling a batch"
" that has already finished returns it unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:289
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`DELETE /v1/batches/{id}` deletes a batch with its requests and results "
"and answers `{\"id\": \"batch_...\", \"object\": \"batch.deleted\", "
"\"deleted\": true}`. Its status does not matter, but deletion is blocked "
"with `409` while any request holds a live upstream lease. Cancel the batch, "
"wait for its running requests to finish (or their leases to expire), then "
"delete it. A stale `running` item whose lease has expired does not block "
"deletion."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:290
msgid ""
"A finished batch is deleted automatically after the deployment's "
"retention period, seven days by default, so collect its results before "
"then."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:293
msgid "List your batches"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:295
msgid ""
"`GET /v1/batches` lists your own batches, newest first. `limit` is 1–100 "
"(default 20); for the next page pass `after` set to the `last_id` of the "
"previous one. The answer has the shape of a results page, with batch "
"objects in `data`."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:300
msgid ""
"Reading, cancelling, deleting and listing your batches work even if your "
"role no longer allows creating them, so you can always collect and remove"
" what you submitted. Another user's batch reads as not found. "
"Administrators may read, cancel and delete any batch."
msgstr ""

